add('A Spirit Power directly and explicitly deals 2 Damage to Dahan; it does not cause a Ravage. Would Defend 3 reduce this Damage? Would Concealing Shadows prevent it? Would Infinite Vitality’s threshold prevent it? Separately, if Invaders Ravage for 2 Damage in a land with Defend 3, how much reaches the land and Dahan?', 'Direct Spirit Power Damage is not reduced by Defend, so those Dahan take 2 Damage in the Defend-only case. Concealing Shadows also does not prevent it because it only protects from Ravaging Invaders. Infinite Vitality’s threshold does prevent that Damage. In the separate Invader Ravage case, Defend 3 reduces 2 to zero for both land and Dahan, not negative Damage.', ['CORE p.18 Defend','Primary card faces: card-scope-source/concealing_shadows.jpg; infinite_vitality.jpg','FAQ Core: .bu6ocxx'], 'Independently accepted Defend source-of-Damage boundary; also isolates non-Ravage Damage from direct Destroy tested by Q117, with exact core protection comparison.')
add('Spirit A has an existing +2 bonus to its Power Ranges and uses Reaching Grasp, whose text grants target Spirit B +2 Range with all their Powers. Does A’s existing bonus increase the amount granted to +4, or does B receive +2? Does B’s Power-only bonus cover Innate Powers as well as Power Cards, and can it extend ordinary Growth placement?', 'The grant stays +2; Range boosts do not increase another Range boost. Reaching Grasp’s Power-only bonus applies to B’s Powers, including Innates and Power Cards, subject to the normal Range-arrow restrictions. It does not extend ordinary Growth, which is not a Power; Power Cards also resolve after normal Growth.', ['Official linked FAQ: card-scope-source/what-do-range-boosts-affect.html/.txt','Primary original Reaching Grasp face: card-scope-source/reaching_grasp.jpg','CORE pp.8,14,16'], 'Explicit not-itself-a-Range-boost condition changes a core Reaching Grasp outcome; maintains Powers-only scope instead of treating every printed arrow as boostable.')
add('For a Range arrow within a Power’s effect text, where is the origin for a land-targeting Power? Where is it for a Spirit-targeting Power used by Spirit A that instructs Spirit B to act? Which Spirit’s Range bonuses apply, and if that internal arrow is Range 1 with A having +2 and B having no bonus, what Range can it reach from whose Presence? How does Blazing Renewal’s explicit measurement origin differ?', 'For a land-targeting Power, measure the internal arrow from the target land unless otherwise specified. For a Spirit-targeting Power, normally measure from the Presence of the Spirit following the instruction, B here, unless the text says otherwise. Apply the bonuses of the Power user A, not B: the stated Range 1 becomes Range 3 from B’s Presence. Blazing Renewal explicitly measures from the Power user A’s Presence, even when B adds Presence; its explicit origin overrides the default.', ['Official linked FAQ: card-scope-source/range-in-text-of-powers-that-target-spirits.html/.txt','Official linked FAQ: card-scope-source/what-do-range-boosts-affect.html/.txt','Primary Blazing Renewal face: card-scope-source/blazing_renewal.jpg'], 'Source-defined internal Range origin branches and Power-user bonus ownership differ; a directly relevant original-core procedure absent from the captured broad category.')
add('A Spirit plays and pays for a Power Card, then foregoes its entire text because it has no legal target or the Spirit chooses not to use it. With no other effect removing the card, do its printed Elements remain available for Innates, is its Energy refunded, and does the card leave play immediately or during Time Passes?', 'Its printed Elements remain while the card is in play and can support Innates even though its text was not used. The paid Energy is not refunded. Foregoing the text does not remove/discard the card immediately; it stays in play and is normally discarded during Time Passes, when its Elements go away.', ['CORE p.17 General Principle You Can Skip Using A Power’s Effect; pp.8,10,16'], 'Independent novelty adjudication accepted retained Elements when the whole Power text is foregone; refund and cleanup clauses are prior regression facts, not extra novelty.')
add('Two separate Ravages occur in the same land before Time Passes. Each would deal 4 Damage before the land’s Defend 3; assume that pre-Defend total stays 4, and one Dahan starts healthy. Is Defend expended on the first Ravage? How much Damage reaches land and Dahan each time? Do the two 1-Damage land results combine into Blight, and what happens to that Dahan on the second Ravage?', 'Defend is not expended: it reduces each Ravage by 3 for the entire turn. Each deals 1 Damage to land and 1 to Dahan. Land Damage below 2 is ignored per occurrence, so the two 1-Damage land results never combine into Blight. The Dahan’s first 1 Damage persists until Time Passes; the second 1 reaches its 2 Health and destroys it before a second counterattack.', ['CORE pp.9,10,16,18 Defend and Damage'], 'Independent novelty adjudication accepted reusable Defend and nonaccumulating land Damage across actions; contrasts persistent piece Damage with ignored partial land Damage.')
assert len(q['questions'])==122
idx=104;oldkey=k['answers'][idx].copy();oldquestion=q['questions'][idx].copy()
k['answers'][idx]['answer']="No. Shadows' conditional targeting ability changes only the numeric Range used to choose the land target, leaving internal Range arrows unchanged. General Power Range bonuses can affect printed Range values in a Power's targeting box and effect text, subject to all restrictions, but do not increase a Range bonus itself and do not apply to another Spirit's Powers merely because they target the boosted Spirit. Neither waives other source/target restrictions."
